{"name":"Capsicum Red","hex":"#76392e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"capsicum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various tropical American plants, of the genus Capsicum, principally the species Capsicum annuum and Capsicum frutescens, that are cultivated as edible peppers.","The non-spicy fruit of the above plants, such as the bell pepper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capsicum"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Capsicum","blocks":[{"text":"Capsicum is a genus of flowering plants in the nightshade family Solanaceae, native to the Americas, cultivated worldwide for their edible fruit, which are generally known as \"peppers\" or \"capsicum\". Chili peppers grow on five species of Capsicum. Sweet or bell peppers and some chili peppers are Capsicum annuum, making it the most cultivated species in the genus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Red_capsicum_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Red_capsicum_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capsicum","wikidata":"Q201959"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Cachi_02.jpg/500px-Cachi_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Cachi_02.jpg/1280px-Cachi_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Cachi_02.jpg/500px-Cachi_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red peppers in Cachi, Argentina air-drying before being processed into powder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACachi_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Arrangement_of_jalape%C3%B1o%2C_banana%2C_cayenne%2C_chili%2C_and_habanero_peppers.jpg/500px-Arrangement_of_jalape%C3%B1o%2C_banana%2C_cayenne%2C_chili%2C_and_habanero_peppers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Arrangement_of_jalape%C3%B1o%2C_banana%2C_cayenne%2C_chili%2C_and_habanero_peppers.jpg/1280px-Arrangement_of_jalape%C3%B1o%2C_banana%2C_cayenne%2C_chili%2C_and_habanero_peppers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Arrangement_of_jalape%C3%B1o%2C_banana%2C_cayenne%2C_chili%2C_and_habanero_peppers.jpg/500px-Arrangement_of_jalape%C3%B1o%2C_banana%2C_cayenne%2C_